From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 10:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] mmdevapi: Preserve shared Sony endpoint properties on startup.

Patch 0019 avoids preloading persisted Sony endpoints so that current driver
enumeration, rather than stale registry records, determines which controllers
are present. However, it also deletes the endpoint's MMDevices registry key.
This runs in every process loading mmdevapi, while the registry is shared.
A second process can therefore delete the properties of an endpoint that the
game has already enumerated and still holds in its process-local device list.

The R2 trace in issue #750 shows this failure in Arknights: Endfield:

  468691.227: PID 0140 opens the controller endpoint
              {1bd72244-d350-40a7-a443-4f2e33b20d56}.
  468694.168-173: PID 0474 loads mmdevapi and removes three persisted
                 DualSense endpoints from the shared registry.
  468706.622 onward: PID 0140 repeatedly fails to read the original
                    endpoint's container ID and device format with error 2.

Replugging publishes a fresh endpoint and allows audio haptics to work. The
initial streams were stopped and released before the registry deletion, so
this change addresses the broken rediscovery/retry path, not the application's
reason for closing those first streams. Absence of the one-second PCM peak
trace on those short-lived streams is not evidence of a stalled audio pump.

Skip persisted Sony endpoints without deleting their shared property stores.
They remain absent from this process's collection until live driver discovery
publishes them, preserving the purpose of 0019. Keep normal-device preloading,
physical hotplug cleanup, routing, controller identity, and Steam Input
selection unchanged. The registry enumeration index must advance normally
because no key is removed from the enumeration.

Bug: https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/750#issuecomment-6126806805
---
 dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c | 8 +++++---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c b/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
--- a/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
+++ b/dlls/mmdevapi/devenum.c
@@ -2012,9 +2012,11 @@
         {
             if (is_dualsense_endpoint_name( pv.pwszVal ))
             {
-                TRACE("Removing persisted DualSense endpoint %s.\n", debugstr_w(pv.pwszVal));
-                if (RegDeleteTreeW(cur, guidvalue) == ERROR_SUCCESS)
-                    i--;
+                /* A different process may still use this shared property store.
+                 * Skip the cached endpoint locally; only live driver discovery
+                 * should publish it in this process. */
+                TRACE("Skipping persisted Sony endpoint %s (%s); keeping shared properties.\n",
+                        debugstr_w(pv.pwszVal), debugstr_guid(&guid));
             }
             else
                 MMDevice_Create(pv.pwszVal, &guid, curflow,
